				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Strip verbose logging and unused imports across Mountain backend\n\nSystematically remove development-time logging noise (`dev_log!`, `println!`) and unused imports (`serde_json::Value`, `tauri::Emitter`, `tokio::time::Instant`) from the Mountain backend source tree.\n\nThis cleanup targets over 400 files across `ApplicationState`, `Binary`, `Command`, `IPC`, `RPC`, `Track`, and `Vine` modules. Key areas affected include:\n- **State Management:** Removed verbose logging from Extension, Configuration, Debug, Terminal, and Workspace state initialization and mutation paths.\n- **IPC & Handlers:** Stripped debug prints from FileSystem, Git, Terminal, and UI service handlers that previously logged every argument and return value.\n- **Cocoon gRPC Services:** Removed per-call logging from Extension, FileSystem, Terminal, and Window service implementations.\n- **Vine Notifications:** Cleaned up notification handlers for Output, Progress, SCM, and Webview events.\n\nThe codebase now relies on structured telemetry (OpenTelemetry spans) and specific error logging rather than high-volume informational prints. This reduces binary size, improves runtime performance by eliminating string formatting overhead, and clarifies the signal-to-noise ratio in production logs.",
			"SHA": "d495abe4f84e4359b7842bf9e2bdce8babd069ca"
